    "case_id": "329",
    "case_summary": "A patient in their 70s presented with dyspnea and fatigue. No history of structural heart disease or hypertension. Medical history significant for diffuse large B-cell lymphoma diagnosed 4 years ago, treated with 8 courses of chemotherapy.\n\nBlood pressure: 96/54 mm HgHeart rate: 56 bpm\n\n- Laboratory Tests:  * Serum troponin I: 0.04 ng/mL (normal value, <0.02 ng/mL)  * NT-proBNP: 3896.83 pg/mL (normal value, <100 pg/mL)- ECG Studies:  Image Title: Findings From Past and Present 12-Lead Electrocardiograms (ECGs)  Image Description: Present ECG shows prolonged P-wave duration (180 milliseconds), positive-negative biphasic P wave in leads II, III, and aVF, with shortened or disappeared PR segment. Compared with ECG from 4 years ago.- Imaging Studies:  * Transthoracic echocardiogram: Revealed diffuse medium masses in the right atrium, measuring approximately 50 mm × 22 mm  * PET-CT scan: Showed significantly increased metabolic activity along the right atrial myocardium and adjacent pericardium",
